# State Management (design SSOT)

State projection primitives (`current_step`, `completed_steps`,
`work_ready_seen_keys`, `pruned_work_ready_buckets`,
`DuplicateWorkDoneHint`, etc.) follow the v3 design walkthrough:

`docs/solutions/state-management/proposal-state-projection-design-walkthrough-v3.md`

## Plan 2026-07-05-005 units (referenced from fix-plan + hardening review)

The 9 implementation Units of `docs/plans/2026-07-05-005-refactor-state-management-hardening-plan.md` and the matching fix-plan (`.ralph/review/2026-07-05-005-refactor-state-management-hardening-plan/fix-plan.md`) shape the runtime. Quick map:

| Unit | File anchor | What it owns |
|------|-------------|--------------|
| U1 — derived `current_step` | `crates/ralph-core/src/step_handoff/progress_task_gate.rs:216` | `ProgressSnapshot::current_step()` returns `completed_steps.last()`; legacy field is read-time-ignored |
| U2 — atomic tasks.jsonl | `crates/ralph-core/src/task_store.rs:77-89` | `write_jsonl_atomic` writes tmp + fsync + rename |
| U3 — projector sees `review.dimensions.complete` | `crates/ralph-core/src/state_projector/*.rs` | New projector action for the U6 completion topic |
| U4 — `DuplicateWorkDone` reason_code (later collapsed by fix-plan U3) | `crates/ralph-core/src/event_policy.rs:174` | Single `duplicate_work_done` code; hint carries the discriminator |
| U5 — `work.ready` dedup counter | `crates/ralph-core/src/event_policy.rs:420` + `573` | `HashMap<String, u32>`; `prune_work_ready_bucket` preserves count via `pruned_work_ready_buckets` side-table |
| U6 — resume-path anchor marker | `crates/ralph-cli/src/commands/resume.rs:215-247` | `write_resume_anchor_marker` writes tmp + fsync + rename |
| U7 — envelope-layer triggered validation | `crates/ralph-cli/src/policy_check.rs:1331-1390` | Topic-trust layering: control / diagnostic topics skip the topology check |
| U8 — shared `check_hat_triggers` helper | `crates/ralph-core/src/workflow_contract/handoff_index.rs` | Single predicate across handoff paths; literal-vs-glob divergence documented at `event_loop/mod.rs:1816-1835` |
| U9 — `ProjectedField<T>` version protocol | (reverted — see fix-plan §U2 + DEC-002) | Dead-on-arrival primitive, revert recommended over half-wiring |

When reading state-management code, start from the v3 walkthrough for the
design intent, then check the matching Unit above for the current contract.